.TH mnnn-net-shard-entrust 1  "mnnn-net-shard-entrust 2.9.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-net\-shard\-entrust \- Split the master key among peers: one sealed shard each, any THRESHOLD restore it
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn net shard entrust\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] <\fB\-\-to\fR> [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-threshold\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-\-words\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-words\-file\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-shard\fR] [\fB\-\-master\-file\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Split the master key among peers: one sealed shard each, any THRESHOLD restore it
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fI<EXCHANGE>\fR
Exchanges or peers (at least two different nodes)
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-threshold\fR \fI<THRESHOLD>\fR [default: 0]
Shards needed to restore (default: a majority, at least 2)
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-words\fR \fI<WORDS>\fR
The 24 recovery words (prefer \-\-words\-file)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-words\-file\fR \fI<WORDS_FILE>\fR
File holding the 24 words (plain text or .age)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-shard\fR \fI<SHARDS>\fR
Shard file (plain text or .age); give at least 3
.TP
\fB\-\-master\-file\fR \fI<MASTER_FILE>\fR
Exported master key file (.age)
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v2.9.0
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmnnn\fR(1)
